  "rule": "Use unchanged V50 amplitude, phase progression and finite cycle-stop mathematics in both fresh walking sessions after the distinct R10I entry guard.",
  "parameter_basis": "V50 passes 362 Rust tests and 26 complete MuJoCo interface/launch checks. Keep every V49 geometry, support, dwell, timeout, amplitude, motor, cycle and stop limit. The startup reference-velocity scalar follows the existing 72-interval smoothstep; position feedback and measured-velocity damping remain active.",
  "compatibility_scope": "The new route selection uses the unchanged V50 native policy/profile/memory/receipt and strict v3 measured-body/floor request in both post-interaction sessions. All historical policy output identities and original diagnostic predicates remain unchanged.",
  "diagnostic_basis": {
    "source_closure": "sdk/development/v50_godot_cycle_stop_closure_v1.json",
    "source_closure_sha256": "sha256:814fcdd31764773984055b788d02618a1086aa379e41a7c0164d550d9709cec7",
    "native_component": "sdk/development/v50_startup_reference_velocity_implementation_v1.json",
    "native_component_sha256": "sha256:edae0114ea3f5e2550bb2db8fb55285997ab326bdbe383fb674e257bd4cdc5f1",
    "physical_outcome_predicted": false,
    "causal_attribution_proven": false
  },
  "physical_acceptance_authority": false,
  "release_authority": false,
  "required_start_profile_id": "r10i_v50_front_left_first_post_interaction_v1",
  "required_walking_policy_id": "r10i_v50_flexed_entry_route_v1",
  "rationale": "One fresh seed-40200 pair through the actual isolated worker, native adapter and cold reader. Common V6 setup and 30-command BW5R-B prefix remain exact. No-kick uses the separate measured-joint flexed entry for at most 240 commands: fresh native memory, zero first actuation, bounded smoothstep to existing V50 under-hip geometry, zero forward/yaw request, completed reference ramp plus 30 consecutive measured-ready samples, explicit session finalization, then fresh V50. Kicked keeps native kick, passive descent, V20/V7 recovery and current readiness guard. Preserve all four planned foot cycles, 120 stopping commands, every native contact/loss and refusal. Test actual producer precision, arm-level handoff linkage, actual recovery-completion phase, command/memory/event linkage and complete independent replay before physics. The new DLL contains a separate entry component and reproduces all 1157 retained V50 native responses byte exactly. No held-out, robustness, equivalence, acceptance or release authority.",
  "predecessor_contract": "sdk/recovery/r10i_v50_walking_entry_contract_v3.json",
  "allowed_evaluation_segments": [
    "walking_resume",
    "matched_continuation"
  ],
  "predecessor_contract_sha256": "sha256:b3edd4b80a9e2c8806652fa11deec509946d0cd05fc9668242991b871f921c4c",
  "integration_revision": "R10I v4 corrects one shared zero-world test exposed by the 669d7405 candidate-walking-frame gate stage: the historical-frame horizon test enumerated the R10G and R10H finite routes but not the R10I flexed route, so it expected the pre-finite 986/1338 step horizon instead of the bound 3160/3512 finite limits. The test now lists the flexed route alongside them. The 669d7405 gate failure is preserved with no physical child. Core, DLL, entry math, runtime command behavior, task criteria and held-out fixtures are unchanged."
